    "teacher_markdown": "## **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n### **Students may assume AI remembers the exact original dataset**\r\n\r\nSome students may expect AI Tutor to perfectly reverse its earlier changes. Encourage them to compare the restored version line by line with the copy they saved in `notes.md` by asking: **\"Did AI restore the exact original data, or did it create something that only looks similar?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant idea:\r\n```markdown\r\nOriginal dataset → Changes → AI attempts restoration\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that generating a plausible earlier version is different from recovering the exact original data.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may focus on the values and overlook structural changes**\r\n\r\nStudents may notice that names or numbers were restored but miss changes to fields, record order, formatting, or data types. Encourage them to compare more carefully by asking: **\"Are the same records, fields, values, and data types all present?\"**\r\n\r\nUseful comparison:\r\n```markdown\r\n- Same number of records?\r\n- Same property names?\r\n- Same values?\r\n- Same data types?\r\n- Same order?\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students evaluate AI output systematically rather than relying on whether it looks correct at first glance.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may think asking AI to \"undo\" is the same as having an actual backup**\r\n\r\nSome students may conclude that an app doesn't need to preserve original data because AI can recreate it. Ask: **\"If the original value is no longer available, how would AI know exactly what it used to be?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant concept:\r\n```javascript\r\nconst originalData = ...\r\n```\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nlet workingData = ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize why applications may preserve an original copy of data before transformations instead of relying on AI to reconstruct lost information.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may not recognize why recording the original matters**\r\n\r\nStudents may see copying the dataset into `notes.md` as an extra step rather than an important part of the experiment. Ask: **\"Without your saved original, how could you tell whether AI restored it accurately?\"**\r\n\r\nThe saved dataset acts as a known reference, allowing students to evaluate AI's claim that it successfully restored the data."
